  "notes": [
    "Historical reconstruction from postgame OpenDota parsing and STRATZ timestamps, not a captured Valve live feed. The seven parsed fight recaps and named kill credits are richer than the currently available live snapshots.",
    "All ten Steam account IDs, hero IDs and sides match across both sources. Score changes and hero deaths use STRATZ death timestamps; kill credits use OpenDota kill logs. The sources sometimes differ by one second, and Radiant has 9 hero kill credits versus 11 scoreboard points. No missing credits are invented.",
    "OpenDota first_blood_time is 157s, matching a Centaur death with no Radiant hero kill credit. The first credited hero kill is Oracle on Enigma at 158s. With no explicit first-blood objective to resolve the discrepancy, this historical preview does not attribute first blood.",
    "Each fight recap uses an explicit OpenDota teamfight segment and its per-player kill/death counts. Segment gold deltas are the sum of all five player gold_delta values per side, not bounty totals, net worth, or proof that combat caused every gold change. All seven segments are included; this is not a claim that every skirmish was parsed.",
    "Building names come from explicit npc_dota building identities. Roshan (Dire, 1744s) and Aegis (Visage, 1745s) come from explicit OpenDota objectives. Courier and Tormentor events are outside this formatter schema and omitted.",
    "Historical net worth is unavailable in these cached responses. OpenDota gold_t is not substituted. Teamfight segment gold changes remain labeled separately from net-worth measurements.",
    "Frames sample every 15 seconds, so messages can trail an event by up to 14 seconds. The exact-duration final frame reports the actual winner; no earlier frame exposes the final result. No Valve delivery or terminal-frame availability is implied."
  ],
